AES-CMAC (SMB3 signing) with the CPU's AES instructions when the compiler targets them (the PS5) or CPUID
reports them: the key expanded once per message. The portable code expands the key again for every
16-byte block and runs AES a byte at a time; a signed transfer from a PS5 ran at about 13 MB/s where FTP
reached 107 MB/s. The portable code stays as the fallback.
smb2_calc_signature runs it over the message's iovecs directly instead of allocating and copying the whole
message for every signature.

--- a/lib/smb2-signing.c	2026-10-30 20:10:21.465298656 +0100
+++ b/lib/smb2-signing.c	2026-10-30 20:29:25.052200190 +0100
